{
  "bridge_text": "寒风轻轻吹动莉娜的红外套，她在那棵大树下屏住呼吸，听见那嗡嗡声竟像是一首古老的歌谣。这阵歌声指引她推开了那扇被冻住的树皮门，踏入那神秘的阴影之中。",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "text": "树干内部盘旋着一圈通往地下的楼梯，台阶尽头坐着一只穿着补丁绿背心的灰狐狸。他叫莫斯克，声音沙哑得像秋日干枯的落叶。他告诉莉娜，这棵树不是让人参观的，让她赶紧回家，忘掉那些扰人的嗡嗡声。可莉娜摇了摇头，她倔强地说，既然还没听完那首歌谣，她怎么能就此离开呢。"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "莫斯克用爪子指了指门口，示意她离开。莉娜却从口袋里掏出了季节里最后的一颗红苹果，轻轻放在他们中间的台阶上，低声说，这是给您带路的辛苦费。莫斯克盯着那颗苹果看了许久，眼神里的严厉渐渐消散。他站起身，理了理那件旧背心，一言不发地向楼梯下方走去。"
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s1"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "Perhaps Mosk holds onto his grumpy secrets because of a heavy heart. As Lina waits on that dusty step, the fox looks down at the apple she offered.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Lina stood firm, her eyes meeting the fox's weary gaze. The humming seemed to vibrate through the wood beneath her feet, a persistent melody that refused to be ignored. Mosk peered at her, his whiskers twitching, and for a moment the air in the hollow tree felt very still."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed at the door, but Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season. She set it on the step between them and said, this is for the trouble of walking me down. Mosk stared at the apple for a long time, his sharp eyes softening just a fraction. Then he stood up, tied his vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a word."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "Mosk may be a grumpy guardian, but even a fox with a heart of dry leaves can be swayed by a kindness. Now, let us see what happens when Lina offers him a gift.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed at the door, but Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season. She set it on the step between them, a small peace offering for the trouble of her visit. Mosk stared at the crisp red fruit for a long time, his nose twitching. Then he stood up, straightened his patched vest, and stepped onto the first stair without another word."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs, the humming grew into a quiet, pulsing song. A firefly the size of a robin lay on a bed of moss, her golden glow flickering and dim. Mosk's whiskers trembled as he looked at her. He whispered that she had been his friend once, but long ago, he had failed to bring her medicine in time. Ever since that winter, he had guarded the tree, far too ashamed to face her."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
