{
  "bridge_text": "With Mosk the fox watching her from his perch in his worn green vest, Lina stood firm against the shadows of the hollow tree. She was ready to hear the secrets hidden deep within the wood.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow tree, a curl of stairs wound deep into the earth. At the very top step sat an old grey fox wearing a patched green vest. His name was Mosk. His voice sounded like dry leaves skittering on stone as he told Lina that this tree was not for visiting. He urged her to go home and forget the humming, but Lina shook her head, insisting she could not forget a song she had not yet heard."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
